1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:03,700
Keeping up with AI news, papers and tools is hard,

2
00:00:03,733 --> 00:00:06,923
and most feeds quietly narrow to what you clicked last week.

3
00:00:06,967 --> 00:00:13,544
Forager keeps me in the loop: a daily brief that stays broad, shows its sources, and asks before it learns.

4
00:00:15,233 --> 00:00:17,512
Setup starts with one sentence about me.

5
00:00:20,100 --> 00:00:24,213
Instead of asking me to write more, Forager splits it into directions

6
00:00:24,267 --> 00:00:30,276
and asks about each with options to click, because recognizing what I want is easier than recalling it.

7
00:00:30,300 --> 00:00:34,163
It suggests nearby fields too, like AI copyright policy,

8
00:00:34,200 --> 00:00:37,112
and offers to follow Sora 2 for two weeks only.

9
00:00:38,933 --> 00:00:41,247
Nothing I don't pick goes into my profile,

10
00:00:41,300 --> 00:00:43,707
and tracking stays off until I turn it on.

11
00:00:43,867 --> 00:00:45,727
Each morning I get a two-layer brief.

12
00:00:45,967 --> 00:00:48,126
Every point cites the items behind it:

13
00:00:48,167 --> 00:00:50,048
click one to check the source myself.

14
00:00:50,800 --> 00:00:52,712
And each item says why it is here:

15
00:00:52,767 --> 00:00:55,447
one of my interests, or breadth I didn't ask for.

16
00:00:59,100 --> 00:01:02,812
From my ratings, Forager may propose a change to my profile,

17
00:01:02,867 --> 00:01:10,473
but it can't write anything itself: the system pauses until I decide, and the evidence comes from code, not the agent's words.

18
00:01:10,500 --> 00:01:15,617
Here the evidence is camera control, a video survey and a video model, not Sora 2,

19
00:01:15,667 --> 00:01:18,420
so I reject it and approve video generation.

20
00:01:22,567 --> 00:01:26,449
Breadth stays visible: no topic may take more than forty percent,

21
00:01:26,500 --> 00:01:28,257
and I set the exploration share.

22
00:01:28,300 --> 00:01:34,877
A manager and three source specialists write it; code checks every digest, and a separate Critic checks meaning.

23
00:01:34,933 --> 00:01:38,763
Here it caught a claim the source never made, and the point was rewritten.

24
00:01:41,233 --> 00:01:49,952
Across thirty recorded digests, the team with rules raised breadth from 23 to about 37 percent, with no loss in relevance.

25
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:55,695
The Critic caught 45 of 48 planted errors, but helped little on real digests.
